release/UNTESTED.md:8:- **Package (A2):** JSON files (by suffix, or text starting with `{` or `[`) are parsed and every key is screened with `credential_key()` (any case or separator, camelCase too), 8+ character string values; the regex stays for other text and now names access/refresh tokens and secret/access keys case-insensitively. Known limit: credentials in YAML, TOML or `.env`-style text under keys the regex does not name; JSON with comments (not parseable) falls back to the regex only.
