release/UNTESTED.md:17:- **Width screen (R14-GPT-03/04):** closed shadow roots are counted at each width after a bounded settle (two animation frames or 250 ms); a viewport that cannot scroll vertically (html, or a propagated body, with `overflow: hidden`/`clip`) fails text and media below its bottom edge unless an inner scroller holds them. UNTESTED: a closed root created later than the settle; `position: sticky` content; horizontal reach on a hidden viewport beyond the existing overflow check.
release/UNTESTED.md:27:- **Width screen (N01-N03, N15, N16):** body overflow that propagates to the viewport, zero-size and `display: contents` wrappers, shadow text clipped by its host, keyboard reach across a table and closed shadow roots (counted through CDP, reported as unscanned) were each reproduced and fixed. UNTESTED: a closed shadow root inside a frame; CDP counting when DevTools domains are unavailable is reported as unscanned, not exercised.
release/UNTESTED.md:28:- **Stylesheets (N07):** `data:` and `blob:` stylesheets are refused; a stylesheet the probe cannot read and the checker did not serve fails. UNTESTED: `@import` chains deeper than one level in shadow roots.
release/UNTESTED.md:29:- **Known limits, raw glass (N08/N09):** `\xNN`, `\uNNNN` and `\u{...}` escapes are decoded and the raw and comment-stripped text are both matched. Not covered (obfuscation, out of the threat model): string concatenation (`'backdrop-' + 'filter'`), `String.fromCharCode`, `atob`, computed property names, template literals assembled at run time, and CSS built from variables in script. The computed-style check and the JavaScript-off pass remain the defences.
release/UNTESTED.md:31:- **Integrity (N11-N14, N19):** the vector now carries every hard-fail input (accent ratios, filler, rule of three, frames, unscanned stylesheets and scopes, per-width maps, contrast unknown/coverage); content compares slot and heading text; a content waiver is INCOMPLETE, never PASS; the native-function check has no default. UNTESTED: JavaScript-off equivalence for content inserted by CSS (`content:` on pseudo-elements).
release/UNTESTED.md:42:- **Integrity (M06-M08, M17):** the full hard-fail vector (glass, h1, placeholders, centred, type sizes, hero gradient, purple-blue, icon rows, accent, spacing off-scale, overflow, clipped, offscreen-left, unreachable, scrolled text, unmeasured, reflow, contrast) is compared page world vs probe world and with JavaScript off, on the positional page and on every declared state. Contrast is a custom diagnostic (text vs resolved solid background, 4.5:1 / 3:1), not axe: axe cannot run with JavaScript off. JavaScript-off content (visible copy slots, h1 count, lang, dir) must match or the cross-check is INCOMPLETE. UNTESTED: text over images or gradients in the contrast diagnostic (counted as unknown, not failed); the native-function check stays a heuristic.
release/UNTESTED.md:43:- **320 px reflow (M01, M02, M09-M11, M14):** scrollers are measured with their own text, open shadow roots and same-origin frames; content outside a scroller's reachable range is `unreachable` at every width; keyboard use means an explicit `tabindex >= 0` scroller or usable targets that step across the whole extent; candidates and their exceptions are scoped to screen/state/lang. UNTESTED: closed shadow roots, `overflow: overlay`, scroll snapping, and whether a resolved candidate genuinely needs 2D layout (the reviewer's decision). *(Superseded in part by R13 N21: same-origin frames are partially inspected and fail the handoff anyway.)*
release/UNTESTED.md:54:- **Glass (S2/C6, panel D):** computed on `html`, `body`, visible elements and rendered pseudo-elements, in open shadow roots and same-origin (srcdoc) frames, plus constructed stylesheets and raw-text scans of served CSS/HTML/SVG/JS, style attributes and `<style>`. Any raw `backdrop-filter` other than `none` fails, even when the rule never applies (fail closed). NOT COVERED: closed shadow roots (unreachable from script) and cross-origin frames (blocked by the checker; listed as `unscannedFrames`). `file://` frames are cross-origin in Chrome, so their glass is caught only by the served-file text scan. A `-webkit-` alias added by a script in a constructed sheet is caught only by that text scan (Chrome drops it when parsing). Styles injected later than the probes run are UNTESTED. *(Superseded by R13 N21: frames are partially inspected and every frame fails the handoff.)*
